<speak>Yes, just a moment. I am not writing a transcript; I am marking where I want to return when I read at home. There, that is done. My family sometimes laughs at how much stationery I still use, but a sheet of paper does not interrupt me with a message. I can put it beside the computer and keep my place. The important thing is not to mistake a personal note for the original document, so I keep the printed material together and the notebook separate.</speak>